 "title": "Heat Shock and Heat Ramp Responses in BY4742 Organism",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on the heat shock and heat ramp responses in the BY4742 organism. The heat ramp process is characterized by its final temperature of 50 °C and its effects on molecular states and nutrient limitation. It is associated with the upregulation of 142 genes and downregulation of 11 genes. The heat shock process also reaches 50 °C and is affected by molecular states and nutrient limitation. It is linked to the upregulation of 142 genes and downregulation of 11 genes. The transcriptome is affected by both heat ramp and heat shock processes. The DEGs and Table S6 are related to the WGCNA method, which applies to bulk transcriptomic datasets and uses ComBat. Stillman B is involved in the DNA replication fork process and published in Annu Rev Biochem.",
